# promise: crash-webkit-tab-closed-entering-fullscreen
# A WebKit tab (a DRM service's, ${WEBKIT} here) closed while its video was still going into full screen: its view came
# down with WebKit's entry pending, WebKit's full-screen controller went away with it, and WebKit stopped Cra on its own
# trap (beganEnterFullScreen) a few seconds later. The view now waits for WebKit, asks it to leave once in, and goes once
# it is out. Closing a tab already in full screen takes the same way. Page races alone (leave while entering, enter
# while leaving) never trapped.
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=900 stalls50=60
pace 0.5
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${WEBKIT}/media.html?n=behind
expect-log loaded localhost \(HTTP 200\)
cra://open?url=${WEBKIT}/media.html?n=entering
wait 3
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1

# Closed 0.1 s after the page asked for full screen, while WebKit is still on its way in.
pace 0.1
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"(document.getElementById('player').requestFullscreen(),'enter')"}
cra://action/closeTab
pace 0.5
expect-log its view waits for WebKit
# WebKit's trap came when its exit finished, seconds later: give it time.
wait 15

# Closed in full screen.
cra://open?url=${WEBKIT}/media.html?n=inside
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"(document.getElementById('player').requestFullscreen(),'enter inside')"}
wait 3
cra://action/closeTab
wait 10
cra://open?url=${WEBKIT}/media.html?n=after
expect-log GET /media.html\?n=after
wait 2
reject-log fault:
